# .dockerignore — what never reaches the app image build context.
#
# Two jobs:
#   1. Speed. Without this file `COPY . .` shipped the whole working tree to
#      the daemon on every build — .git, backups/, the Android/iOS shells, and
#      (fatally) any host node_modules, which then OVERWROTE the node_modules
#      pnpm had just installed inside the image.
#   2. Correctness of the rebuild fast path. deploy/lib/build.sh fingerprints
#      the source and skips `docker compose build` when the running image was
#      already built from exactly that source. That is only sound because a
#      path listed here provably cannot change the image — so this list and
#      image_context_excludes() in deploy/lib/build.sh must stay in sync
#      (deploy/lib/build.test.sh asserts they do).
#
# NOTE: .env is deliberately NOT ignored. vite.config.ts sets envDir to the
# project root, so VITE_* values (VITE_POS_ANDROID_URL, VITE_DEFAULT_TENANT_SLUG,
# …) are baked into the frontend bundle at build time and the build needs the
# file. build.sh folds .env into the fingerprint for the same reason.

# ── VCS / CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github

# ── Installed + generated artifacts (the image builds its own) ────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
coverage
out

# ── Mobile shells: built by codemagic, not by this image ──────────────────────
android
ios

# ── Ops, docs and tooling that the image never runs ───────────────────────────
deploy
docs
e2e
backups
references
tools
Caddyfile
docker-compose.yml
codemagic.yaml
update.sh
**/*.md

# ── Tests: vite/esbuild never bundle them ─────────────────────────────────────
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
